/*
# SearchField

A text field for searching, that a screen reader announces as a search field, with "Search"
as its placeholder until you give it your own. Its look is the theme's: a stadium — round at
both ends, `searchFieldCornerRadius = "round"` — unless the theme gives that token a radius (a
square-cornered house style gives it its `fieldCornerRadius`), with `searchFieldHeight`, `searchFieldPadding`, and
`searchFieldFill` and `searchFieldStroke` (the theme's `surface` and `line` when unset).
Everything else is `TextInput`'s: `value`, `admit`, `commit`, `onEnter`.

```declare
App [ width = 400, height = 100, q: string = "",
    find: SearchField [ x = 20, y = 20, width = 260, placeholder = "Search messages",
        value <-> app.q ],
    Text [ x = 20, y = 64, text = { app.q == "" ? "type to search" : "searching for " + app.q } ]
    ]
```

## placeholder
"Search" unless you name what is searched ("Search messages") — it is also the field's name to
a screen reader when no `accessibilityLabel` is set.

## height
The theme's `searchFieldHeight`.

## cornerRadius
The theme's `searchFieldCornerRadius`: `"round"` (the default) for round ends at any height, or
a radius, capped at half the height.

## padding
The theme's `searchFieldPadding` at each end, so the text sits clear of round ends.

## fill
The theme's `searchFieldFill`, else its `surface`.

## stroke
The theme's `searchFieldStroke`, else its `line`, turning to its `accent` while the field has
the focus.
*/

include [ "textinput.declare" ]

class SearchField extends TextInput [ height = { provided("theme").searchFieldHeight },
    // round at both ends (the theme's "round", the default), or the radius the theme gives

    cornerRadius = { typeof provided("theme").searchFieldCornerRadius == "number" ? Math.min(provided("theme").searchFieldCornerRadius, height / 2) : height / 2 },
    accessibilityRole = searchBox,
    placeholder = "Search",
    padding = { [0, provided("theme").searchFieldPadding, 0, provided("theme").searchFieldPadding] },
    fill = { provided("theme").searchFieldFill ?? provided("theme").surface },
    stroke = { stroke(1, this.focused ? provided("theme").accent : (provided("theme").searchFieldStroke ?? provided("theme").line)) }
    ]
